Third-party data
----------------
The Olist marketplace demo uses the "Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset by Olist"
(https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/olistbr/brazilian-ecommerce), downloaded from
https://github.com/olist/work-at-olist-data. The dataset is licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/).

The raw dataset is not stored in this repository; `python run.py` downloads it.
The repository contains aggregate research results computed from it (outputs/,
baselines/), and the container image also contains a database derived from it
(data/marketplace.duckdb). Those derived files are distributed under
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, not under the MIT License: they may be used
only for non-commercial purposes, with attribution to Olist, and any adaptation of
them must be shared under the same licence. Changes made to the original data:
tables were loaded into DuckDB, joined, aggregated and filtered as described in
sql/01-07, and unused tables were removed from the runtime database.

MIERU is a non-commercial portfolio and academic project.

The synthetic demonstration files in demo/ and frontend/public/samples/ describe a
fictional company and fictional customers.
